     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p17-subsets-definition",
     "replacement": "The number of ways to arrange $r$ objects chosen from $n$ distinct objects, without repetition, is written ${}^{n}P_r$, where $n$ and $r$ are whole numbers with $0\\leq r\\leq n$.\n\n${}^{n}P_r=\\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!}$\n\n${}^{n}P_n=n!$\n\n${}^{n}P_0=1$",
     "autoApply": true,
